meta {
  name: Get Agency Setup
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/setup
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{onboardOwnerAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("is pending for a freshly onboarded agency", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().status).to.equal("pending");
    expect(res.getBody().completedAt).to.equal(null);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /agency/setup — where this agency is in its first-run setup (PAC-69)

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `agency:branding:read`
  - **Data scope:** the caller's own agency (`@SkipBranch()`).

  ## Why `agency:branding:*` rather than a new permission
  This gates a wizard whose only writes *are* branding and sender-identity
  writes, so anyone who can do the work can say they are finished. A new
  `agency:setup:*` string would have to be granted to every existing owner role
  before the feature worked for anyone — the argument PAC-79 made for reusing
  `agency:users:write`.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  { "status": "pending", "completedAt": null, "brandingSkipped": false }
  ```

  `complete` is the default for every agency **not** created through the panel —
  migrated, seeded and demo tenants have nothing to be walked through. Note a
  stored document predating this feature has no `setup` sub-document at all and
  reads as complete; `.lean()` does not apply the schema default, so readers
  null-guard rather than trusting it.

  ## Errors
  - `403 Forbidden` — lacks `agency:branding:read` (a producer, or a platform
    account, which holds no agency permissions).
}
